**Concern:** `RecordReadFailure` ignores all `OperationCanceledException` instances (including `TaskCanceledException`), which also suppresses transport-originated timeouts and synchronous `Read` cancellations.

In .NET, `TaskCanceledException` inherits from `OperationCanceledException` and is thrown for HTTP/transport timeouts (often wrapping `TimeoutException`, or triggered by an inner timeout/resilience handler on `IHttpClientBuilder` — which `AddPostHogOpenAIClient` explicitly exposes for customization — or an HTTP/2 abort while the caller's read `CancellationToken` is not cancelled). Additionally, synchronous `TrackingStream.Read(byte[], int, int)` (line 690) accepts no `CancellationToken`, so an `OperationCanceledException`/`TaskCanceledException` there cannot be caller-token cancellation on that read.

**Observed vs expected (verified in base `ea79fc9e` and head `1aa457f2` mock-service harness):**
- **Trigger:** An inner stream throws `new TaskCanceledException("The request was canceled due to the configured HttpClient.Timeout of 100 seconds elapsing.", new TimeoutException())` after a partial SSE chunk while the caller's read token is not cancelled (async `ReadToEndAsync`) or via sync `ReadToEnd`.
- **Actual (base & head):** `TaskCanceledException` propagates to the caller, while `$ai_generation` is emitted with `$ai_http_status: 200`, partial output (`"Hel"`), and neither `$ai_is_error` nor `$ai_error` (reporting the failed stream as a success).
- **Expected:** Only caller-initiated cancellations skip `$ai_is_error`; non-caller `OperationCanceledException`/`TaskCanceledException` timeouts record `$ai_is_error: true` and `$ai_error`.
- *(Scope note: under default `OpenAIClient` `ResponseHeadersRead`, `HttpClient.Timeout` ends at headers and `System.ClientModel`'s `NetworkTimeout` wraps `TrackingStream` externally via its own token, so this primarily affects inner timeout/resilience handlers, custom inner handlers/streams, HTTP/2 aborts, and sync `Read`.)*

**Recommendation:** Consider passing `CancellationToken` into `RecordReadFailure` (`CancellationToken.None` from `Read`, `cancellationToken` from `ReadAsync`) and excluding only caller-initiated cancellations:

```csharp
private bool RecordReadFailure(Exception ex, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
{
    var isCallerCancellation =
        ex is OperationCanceledException
        && cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested
        && ex.InnerException is not TimeoutException;

    if (!isCallerCancellation && _streamError == null)
    {
        _streamError = JsonValue.Create(ex.Message);
    }

    return false;
}
```

**Regression test sketch (unexecuted as an xUnit test in checkout; same behavior confirmed via standalone `.NET 8` harness against `sdk-mock-server` on base `ea79fc9e` and head `1aa457f2`):**

```csharp
[Theory]
[InlineData(false)]
[InlineData(true)]
public async Task SendAsyncMarksStreamTimeoutTaskCanceledExceptionAsErrorAndRethrows(bool useSyncRead)
{
    var requestBody = new { model = "gpt-4", messages = new[] { new { role = "user", content = "Say hi" } }, stream = true };
    var sse = "data: {\"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": {\"content\": \"Hel\"}}]}\n\n";
    var timeoutEx = new TaskCanceledException("The request was canceled due to the configured HttpClient.Timeout of 100 seconds elapsing.", new TimeoutException());
    var streamContent = new StreamContent(new FailingAfterBytesStream(new UTF8Encoding(false).GetBytes(sse), () => timeoutEx));
    streamContent.Headers.ContentType = new MediaTypeHeaderValue("text/event-stream");
    _innerHandler.Response = new HttpResponseMessage(HttpStatusCode.OK) { Content = streamContent };

    using var requestContent = new StringContent(JsonSerializer.Serialize(requestBody), Encoding.UTF8, "application/json");
    HttpResponseMessage? response = null;
    try
    {
        using var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, new Uri("/v1/chat/completions", UriKind.Relative)) { Content = requestContent };
        response = await _client.SendAsync(request, HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead);
        var resultStream = await response.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();
        using var reader = new StreamReader(resultStream);
        if (useSyncRead) Assert.Throws<TaskCanceledException>(() => reader.ReadToEnd());
        else await Assert.ThrowsAsync<TaskCanceledException>(() => reader.ReadToEndAsync());
    }
    finally
    {
        response?.Dispose();
    }

    _postHogClient.Received(1).Capture(
        Arg.Any<string>(),
        PostHogAIFieldNames.Generation,
        Arg.Is<Dictionary<string, object>>(props =>
            props.ContainsKey(PostHogAIFieldNames.IsError)
            && (bool)props[PostHogAIFieldNames.IsError]
            && props.ContainsKey(PostHogAIFieldNames.Error)
        ),
        null, false, Arg.Any<DateTimeOffset?>()
    );
}
```

**Concern:** Both guard branches added in `RecordReadFailure` (`ex is not OperationCanceledException` and `_streamError == null`) currently have no unit test coverage.

**Expected contract & evidence:** `src/PostHog.AI/PostHogOpenAIHandler.cs:761` introduces two distinct behavioral guarantees beyond the `IOException` path: (1) caller-initiated cancellation is excluded from `$ai_is_error`/`$ai_error`, and (2) an earlier upstream SSE error chunk (such as `data: {"error":{"message":"upstream failed"}}\n\n` or `response.failed`) is preserved rather than overwritten if the underlying transport subsequently drops. Neither branch is exercised in `PostHogOpenAIHandlerTests.cs:470-554` (so removing either condition would still pass the test suite).

**Recommendation:** Consider generalizing `FailingAfterBytesStream` to accept a `Func<Exception>` factory and adding unit tests for:
1. Caller-cancelled `OperationCanceledException` (with cancelled caller `CancellationToken`) -> rethrown, `$ai_is_error` and `$ai_error` omitted.
2. Non-caller timeout `TaskCanceledException` (paired with the `RecordReadFailure` concern) -> rethrown, `$ai_is_error: true` and `$ai_error` set.
3. SSE `{"error": ...}` chunk followed by `IOException("connection reset")` -> `IOException` rethrown, `$ai_is_error: true`, and `$ai_error` retains `"upstream failed"` rather than `"connection reset"`.

**Test sketch (unexecuted as xUnit tests in checkout; both behaviors confirmed via standalone `.NET 8` harness against `sdk-mock-server` on head `1aa457f2`):**

```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task SendAsyncDoesNotMarkCallerCancelledStreamAsError()
{
    var requestBody = new { model = "gpt-4", messages = new[] { new { role = "user", content = "Say hi" } }, stream = true };
    var sse = "data: {\"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"delta\": {\"content\": \"Hel\"}}]}\n\n";
    using var cts = new CancellationTokenSource();
    var streamContent = new StreamContent(
        new FailingAfterBytesStream(new UTF8Encoding(false).GetBytes(sse), () => { cts.Cancel(); return new OperationCanceledException(cts.Token); })
    );
    streamContent.Headers.ContentType = new MediaTypeHeaderValue("text/event-stream");
    _innerHandler.Response = new HttpResponseMessage(HttpStatusCode.OK) { Content = streamContent };

    using var requestContent = new StringContent(JsonSerializer.Serialize(requestBody), Encoding.UTF8, "application/json");
    HttpResponseMessage? response = null;
    try
    {
        using var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, new Uri("/v1/chat/completions", UriKind.Relative)) { Content = requestContent };
        response = await _client.SendAsync(request, HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead);
        var resultStream = await response.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();
        var buffer = new byte[1024];
        _ = await resultStream.ReadAsync(buffer, cts.Token);
        await Assert.ThrowsAsync<OperationCanceledException>(() => resultStream.ReadAsync(buffer, cts.Token).AsTask());
    }
    finally
    {
        response?.Dispose();
    }

    _postHogClient.Received(1).Capture(
        Arg.Any<string>(),
        PostHogAIFieldNames.Generation,
        Arg.Is<Dictionary<string, object>>(props =>
            !props.ContainsKey(PostHogAIFieldNames.IsError) && !props.ContainsKey(PostHogAIFieldNames.Error)
        ),
        null, false, Arg.Any<DateTimeOffset?>()
    );
}

[Fact]
public async Task SendAsyncPreservesSseErrorWhenStreamSubsequentlyDrops()
{
    var requestBody = new { model = "gpt-4", messages = new[] { new { role = "user", content = "Say hi" } }, stream = true };
    var sse = "data: {\"error\":{\"message\":\"upstream failed\",\"type\":\"server_error\"}}\n\n";
    var streamContent = new StreamContent(
        new FailingAfterBytesStream(new UTF8Encoding(false).GetBytes(sse), () => new IOException("connection reset"))
    );
    streamContent.Headers.ContentType = new MediaTypeHeaderValue("text/event-stream");
    _innerHandler.Response = new HttpResponseMessage(HttpStatusCode.OK) { Content = streamContent };

    using var requestContent = new StringContent(JsonSerializer.Serialize(requestBody), Encoding.UTF8, "application/json");
    HttpResponseMessage? response = null;
    try
    {
        using var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, new Uri("/v1/chat/completions", UriKind.Relative)) { Content = requestContent };
        response = await _client.SendAsync(request, HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead);
        var resultStream = await response.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();
        using var reader = new StreamReader(resultStream);
        await Assert.ThrowsAsync<IOException>(() => reader.ReadToEndAsync());
    }
    finally
    {
        response?.Dispose();
    }

    _postHogClient.Received(1).Capture(
        Arg.Any<string>(),
        PostHogAIFieldNames.Generation,
        Arg.Is<Dictionary<string, object>>(props =>
            (bool)props[PostHogAIFieldNames.IsError]
            && props[PostHogAIFieldNames.Error].ToString()!.Contains("upstream failed", StringComparison.Ordinal)
            && !props[PostHogAIFieldNames.Error].ToString()!.Contains("connection reset", StringComparison.Ordinal)
        ),
        null, false, Arg.Any<DateTimeOffset?>()
    );
}
```
